<title>PAKISTAN: KARACHI PORT HANDLES 91,734 TONNES CARGO.</title>
<headline>KARACHI PORT HANDLES 91,734 TONNES CARGO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 91,734 tonnes of export and import</p>
<p>cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday, compared to 68,076 tonnes on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Saturday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			  4,680	    9,320</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  87,054	   58,756</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships are expected to sail and eight to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to</p>
<p>unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas		     51,000	 Warba		  due</p>
<p>Crude oil	     65,000	 Captain Mirnada    11/8</p>
<p>Veg Oil		 18,600	 Kristal		due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
